here to material owned by another person.

By exercising a right granted by this license, you accept and agree to comply
with its terms. If you exercise rights for an organization, you represent
that you are authorized to do so and that the organization will comply with
these terms to the extent applicable law permits.

Definitions

"Licensor" means Nguyễn Lê Văn Dũng, solely for rights the Licensor owns or is
authorized to license.

"Covered Material" means the original Soma source code, build scripts,
documentation, text, graphics, and original Soma code in official application
builds compiled and distributed by the Licensor, as identified in NOTICE, but
only to the extent copyright exists in that material and is owned or
controlled by the Licensor. It excludes third-party material and material
authored by another contributor unless that contributor has separately
granted the Licensor the necessary rights in writing. NOTICE and the
applicable third-party license files identify separate material and its
terms.

"Official Build" means an unmodified compiled Soma application built by the
Licensor and released by the Licensor or with the Licensor's written
authorization as an official Soma build. Redistributing an unchanged copy
does not change its status as an Official Build. A build compiled or modified
by another person is not an Official Build.

"Forked Build" means any compiled Soma application built by someone other
than the Licensor from the Covered Material, whether or not it is modified.

"Learner Charge" means any required payment or other consideration, whether
paid by a learner or by someone on the learner's behalf, that is tied to
instruction, enrollment, participation, assessment, a credential, course
materials, or access to a course, program, or educational service using the
Covered Material. A charge remains a Learner Charge regardless of its name,
recipient, collection method, or whether it is bundled with another charge.
A genuinely optional contribution, with no effect on access or treatment, is
not a Learner Charge. General public funding or taxes, including public
subsidies allocated per learner, are not a Learner Charge unless the learner,
their family, or a private sponsor must pay that amount as a condition of
access.

"End-User Charge" means any required payment or other consideration, whether
paid directly by an end user or on their behalf, that is required to access
or use the Covered Material, the Soma application, or a product, service,
course, or other activity in which it is used, supplied, or materially relied
upon. It includes tuition, access fees, subscriptions, required donations,
and amounts bundled under another name, regardless of who collects the
payment or how it is routed. A genuinely optional contribution with no effect
on access is not an End-User Charge. General public funding or taxes are not
an End-User Charge unless payment by the end user or a private sponsor is a
condition of access.

"Community Research" means research primarily intended to benefit the public
or a community, rather than a business's commercial interests. It must not be
commissioned, directed, controlled, or funded by a business; create exclusive
commercial rights or deliverables for a business; or be intended to develop,
support, or improve a paid product or service. Results must be made available
to the public without a fee no later than twelve months after the research is
completed, and before any commercial use of those results. Public or
charitable grants and ordinary academic salaries alone do not make research
commercial.

1. Limited free permission

Subject to every term of this license, the Licensor grants you a limited,
worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free
copyright license to use the Covered Material as follows:

   a. You may download, install, and run an unmodified Official Build for
      education, personal self-study, or Community Research. A Learner Charge
      or End-User Charge for the broader education, self-study, or research
      program or service does not by itself make this Official Build use
      commercial. This permission does not allow you to sell, rent, or
      separately charge for access to the Official Build itself.

   b. You may reproduce and modify the Covered Material to build, install,
      run, and share a Forked Build for education, personal self-study, or
      Community Research only if no End-User Charge is imposed for access to
      or use of that Forked Build or a service in which it is used.

This permission covers only the Licensor's copyright in the Covered Material.
It does not grant patent, trademark, publicity, or other rights. Uses that
applicable law permits without a license are not restricted by this license.

2. Paid and other commercial use requires prior permission

Except for the Official Build use expressly permitted by Section 1(a), any
use intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or private monetary
compensation requires a separate paid commercial license signed by the
Licensor before that use begins, including by a legally valid electronic
signature. The fee and scope must be stated in that agreement. There is no
free commercial trial period. A public repository, download, attribution, or
permission from a third party is not that authorization.

For every Forked Build, the person building, operating, or distributing it
must determine whether an End-User Charge is imposed. If any End-User Charge
is imposed, the use is commercial regardless of its stated purpose, payment
route, payer, recipient, or fee structure. That charge-bearing Forked Build
must remain disabled and unavailable to end users until the Licensor approves
the use in writing and signs a paid commercial license. A Forked Build
without an End-User Charge is permitted without that approval only for the
uses and under the conditions in Section 1(b).

An Official Build may be used free of charge for the purposes in Section
1(a), even when a learner or end user is charged for the broader education,
self-study, or research program or service. This exception does not permit a
separate fee for the Official Build itself or any other commercial use
outside Section 1(a).

Commercial use includes, without limitation:

   a. Education using a Forked Build when a Learner Charge or End-User Charge
      is imposed. This does not include broader program or service charges
      for an Official Build use permitted by Section 1(a).

   b. Research commissioned, directed, controlled, or funded by a business;
      research whose results or rights are reserved for a business; or
      research intended to create, support, test, or improve a product or
      service offered for payment or commercial advantage.

   c. Using the Covered Material to create, provide, operate, support, or
      market a product, service, or activity for revenue, private monetary
      compensation, or material commercial advantage, whether or not the
      Covered Material itself is sold or separately charged for. This
      includes paid access, subscriptions, advertising, sponsorship tied to
      access, fees, sales, and monetized online services, except for an
      Official Build use expressly permitted by Section 1(a).

The actual arrangement and purpose control; labels, organizational form,
country, charitable or public status, an Official Build, a free download, or
routing payment through an affiliate, contractor, reseller, sponsor, parent,
or other intermediary do not change the use's character. A person using the
Covered Material on behalf of, at the direction of, or for the material
commercial benefit of another party must obtain the permission required for
that use.

3. Sharing and attribution

You may redistribute an unmodified Official Build without charging a separate
fee for the app, only for a use allowed by Section 1(a). Broader educational
program or service charges do not by themselves restrict that redistribution.
You may distribute a Forked Build only for a use allowed by Section 1(b),
without an End-User Charge. Each copy must include this license and preserve
the Copyright Notice and Source Notice. Each recipient's permission comes
directly from the Licensor under this license and is independently subject to
its terms; you may not grant a recipient broader rights or represent that you
can authorize commercial use.

When the Covered Material is used in an application or service, visibly credit
Nguyễn Lê Văn Dũng as the original creator of Soma and Licensor of the Covered
Material, and include the Source Notice in an About, credits, or equivalent
area. Modified copies must clearly identify that they were changed and must
not imply that the Licensor endorses them. Do not remove, obscure, or replace
required copyright, source, or third-party notices.

